<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert F. Kennedy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1925">1925</a>–<a href="/years/1968">1968</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Robert Francis Kennedy, RFK</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Francis Kennedy was an American politician and lawyer who served as the 64th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> attorney general from 1961 to 1964 and as a senator from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> from 1965 until his assassination in 1968. He managed the campaigns of his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-f-kennedy">John F. Kennedy</a> and was his closest adviser, and as attorney general he supported the civil rights movement and fought organized crime. As a senator he opposed US involvement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a> and sponsored legislation against poverty. A leading candidate for the Democratic presidential nomination in 1968, he was shot by Sirhan Sirhan shortly after winning the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> primary and died 25 hours later.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-f-kennedy.jpg" alt="Robert F. Kennedy" width="330" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harry Warnecke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_F._Kennedy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
